<title>JAPAN: Nissan Oct domestic output down 5.6% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Nissan Oct domestic output down 5.6% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nissan Motor Co Ltd said on Wednesday that its domestic vehicle production, exports, domestic sales and overseas output in October were as follows (comparisons are with a year earlier):</p>
<p> Production	  132,698   down 5.6 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars	     116,551   down 5.3 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses  16,147   down 7.8 percent</p>
<p> Domestic sales     76,411   down 8.4 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		55,457   down 8.8 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses  20,954   down 7.2 percent</p>
<p> Exports		48,839   up   3.2 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		41,413   up   1.6 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses   7,426   up  13.4 percent</p>
<p> Overseas output   115,379   up  19.1 percent</p>
<p>Nissan's domestic vehicle production fell in October for the third straight month year-on-year, reflecting slow domestic sales. Domestic vehicle sales marked the second straight year-on-year decline.</p>
<p>Its overseas production gained for the fourth successive month, mainly due to higher output at its Mexican unit.</p>
<p>Its exports rose for a second straight month, helped by higher U.S. demand for its Pathfinder and other new models.</p>
</text>
